 our journey, we have built a strong relationship of trust with our clients. Here you will find answers to the most frequently asked questions.","viewAll":"View All","question1":"Can I register without a Palestinian ID number?","answer1":"Yes, you can register using a non-Palestinian identification document such as a passport. Upon registration, you must select the correct document type from the list. However, registering with a Palestinian ID number is preferred for verification purposes.","question2":"Why does the system show that my ID number is invalid or not nine digits, even though it is correct?","answer2":"Please ensure that there are no spaces before or after the ID number when entering it. The platform does not accept ID numbers that contain spaces.","question3":"If I am a job seeker but currently outside Palestine, can I register on the platform?","answer3":"Yes, you can register from anywhere. The platform is available for all Palestinians worldwide.","question4":"I entered my mobile number but did not receive the verification code. What should I do?","answer4":"You must wait 1–3 minutes for the verification code to arrive. If more than five minutes pass, try registering again and make sure that the number is correct, contains 10 digits, and that the country code is accurate.","question5":"I tried several times but still did not receive the verification code.","answer5":"Some numbers block messages from platforms due to advertisement filtering. This can be resolved by contacting your mobile operator or by using a different number.","question6":"What happens if I attempt registration many times?","answer6":"You have five attempts to register. After that, the system will lock your ID number for one hour before you can try again.","question7":"How do I set my password, and can I change it?","answer7":"After entering the verification code, you will be asked to create and confirm your password. Please follow the password requirements shown on the page.","question8":"I am sure my ID number is correct, but the system says I do not meet the criteria.","answer8":"The platform only allows registration for individuals aged 16 and above, which is the legal working age according to labor laws.","question9":"When does my account become inactive?","answer9":"If you do not log in for more than six months, your account becomes inactive and you must log in once for it to reactivate. While inactive, you will not appear in employer matching results.","question10":"Can I register without entering my education, skills, and experience information?","answer10":"Yes, you can register without entering this information. However, leaving these fields empty will reduce your chances of appearing in job matching results, as the matching engine relies on your entered data.","question11":"Are all fields mandatory, or can I leave some empty?","answer11":"Matching depends on the completeness and accuracy of your information. The more accurate and complete your profile is, the higher your chances of finding suitable opportunities.","question12":"Am I required to upload documents during registration?","answer12":"Documents are only mandatory if you register without a Palestinian ID number, in which case you must upload a document proving your identity. Other documents such as CVs, certificates, and experience letters are optional but recommended to improve your chances.","question13":"How will I know if an employer has selected me?","answer13":"Employers cannot view your personal documents due to privacy policies, but they can see your email address and mobile number to contact you if needed.","question14":"Can employers see my uploaded documents?","answer14":"No. Privacy policies strictly prevent any user from viewing documents you upload to the platform.","question15":"Will I be notified about job postings that match my skills and experience?","answer15":"Yes, you will receive daily email notifications with suitable job opportunities.","question16":"Is entering an email address mandatory?","answer16":"No, but if you add an email address, you will receive daily notifications of relevant job postings.","question17":"Can I update or modify my information later?","answer17":"Yes, you can update your data at any time through your profile page, where many editing options are available.","question18":"Can I upload a profile picture?","answer18":"Yes, you may upload and update your profile picture at any time.","question19":"How can I apply to job postings on the platform?","answer19":"You must have a registered account to view application instructions. Each job posting includes a specific link that directs you to the employer or advertiser to complete the application process.","question20":"What should I do if I face issues with registration, uploading documents, or searching on the platform?","answer20":"The platform provides several support channels, including: – A dedicated support page with contact persons – Email support – A contact form on the website – The official Facebook page, where you will receive a response within 24–48 hours.","question21":"Why does the system tell me that my account needs verification and that I must wait 24–48 hours?","answer21":"If you register using a non-Palestinian ID, the platform must manually review your uploaded document to prevent identity fraud. If you register with a Palestinian ID, verification is automatic.","question22":"Why must I enter the ID issuance date when selecting a Palestinian ID?","answer22":"To prevent identity fraud and due to integration with the Ministry of Interior, the system requires the issuance date to verify ownership of the ID.","question23":"What can lead to my account being suspended?","answer23":"Providing false or misleading information, violating the terms of use or privacy policy, posting job ads that violate labor laws, or using offensive language anywhere on the platform.","question24":"What if a job posting turns out to be fraudulent or illegal after I apply?","answer24":"All job postings must comply with labor regulations and be from legitimate and registered entities in Palestine. If any violation occurs, users should report it through all available reporting options on the platform.","question25":"What are the allowed salary ranges for posted jobs?","answer25":"The Ministry of Labour does not allow job postings with wages below the minimum wage of 1,880 NIS per month. Employers and candidates may negotiate the final salary, but any wage below the minimum must be reported.","question26":"What if an employer asks for my ID number or bank account details?","answer26":"The Ministry strictly advises users NOT to provide personal information such as ID numbers, passport numbers, bank account details, or exact residential addresses. Such information should only be shared after signing an employment contract.","question27":"What is required to register as an employer on the platform?","answer27":"You must select your employer type and enter your registration number—such as a company registration number from the Ministry of Economy, an association registration number from the Ministry of Interior, or a tax file number from the Ministry of Finance. You must also upload a registration document (e.g., company registration certificate, tax file, profession license, association certificate) to verify the employer's information. The person registering the employer must enter their personal ID number to link them to the employer account.","question28":"What is required if I choose \\"Company registered with the Ministry of Economy\\"?","answer28":"You must enter the company registration number (verified through the Ministry of Economy) and upload the official company registration certificate.","question29":"How long does it take to activate an employer account before posting jobs?","answer29":"If registration occurs during official working hours, verification and activation will be completed on the same day. If registration occurs during weekends or holidays, activation will take place on the next working day."},"sectionJobsView":{"titleBold":"Dozens of Jobs","titleRest":"Available","titleSubtitle":"Apply for the job that matches your skills","description1":"Browse dozens of available jobs and choose the one that matches your skills","description2":"You will find a large number of jobs offered through the site and companies in various fields to reach your dream job or develop your current skills and training opportunities","listItem1":"Large number of available jobs","listItem2":"Large number of business sectors","listItem3":"Training opportunities for new graduates","companiesCount":"More than {count} employers","companiesCountDefault":"More than +300 employers"},"userFeedback":{"title":"Share Your Feedback","description":"Help us improve the JobMatch platform by sharing your opinion and rating","steps":{"rating":"Rating","featureSelection":"Feature Selection","comments":"Additional Comments"},"nps":{"question":"How likely are you to recommend JobMatch platform to a friend or colleague?","notLikely":"Not Likely","veryLikely":"Very Likely","errors":{"required":"Please select an NPS rating","invalid":"Rating must be between 0 and 10"}},"features":{"question":"Which of the following features would you like to see developed in the next phase?","errors":{"required":"Please select at least one feature"}},"comments":{"question":"Do you have any additional comments or suggestions to improve the platform?","placeholder":"Write your comments or suggestions here..."},"buttons":{"previous":"Previous","next":"Next","submit":"Submit Feedback","submitting":"Submitting...","submitted":"Thank you for your contribution!"},"errors":{"completeFields":"Please complete the required fields","submitFailed":"An error occurred while submitting your feedback. Please try again."},"success":"Thank you for your contribution! Your feedback has been recorded."},"newsAndEvents":{"title":"News and Events","